                    <!-- MIS 325 ride share database: my own SQL (HW 4, question 3) in an editor frame instead of a screenshot -->
                    <div class="mp-proj" id="mp-proj-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="mp-rideshare-db" hidden>
                    <div class="mp-proof">
                        <div class="mp-code">
                            <div class="mp-code-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><em>hw4.sql</em></div>
<pre><code><span class="c">-- Average fare per rider, highest first</span>
<span class="k">SELECT</span> r.rider_id,
       r.first_name,
       r.last_name,
       <span class="k">ROUND</span>(<span class="k">AVG</span>(ri.final_fare), <span class="n">2</span>) <span class="k">AS</span> avg_fare
<span class="k">FROM</span> rider r
<span class="k">JOIN</span> ride ri
  <span class="k">ON</span> r.rider_id = ri.rider_id
<span class="k">GROUP BY</span> r.rider_id, r.first_name, r.last_name
<span class="k">ORDER BY</span> avg_fare <span class="k">DESC</span>;</code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="mp-eyebrow">Built, not just studied · MIS 325 · Database Management</p>
                            <h3 id="mp-rideshare-db">Ride Share Database</h3>
                            <p class="mp-proof-sub">Where RideFlow started. Before it was an app, it was a database: riders, drivers, vehicles, rides, payments and discounts, designed and queried in Oracle SQL.</p>
                            <ul class="mp-facts">
                                <li><b>8</b><span>TABLES</span></li>
                                <li><b>9</b><span>FOREIGN KEYS</span></li>
                                <li><b>9</b><span>CHECK RULES</span></li>
                                <li><b>13</b><span>QUERIES</span></li>
                            </ul>
                            <ul class="mp-proof-list">
                                <li>A schema built from scratch, with ID sequences, keys and check constraints enforcing the business rules</li>
                                <li>Sample data loaded and indexed for the queries that run most</li>
                                <li>Queries using joins, GROUP BY and HAVING, subqueries, and ROLLUP and CUBE subtotals</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
